  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3229.07 Handlebars",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3229.07 Handlebars.\n\n(a) The handlebars of each motorcycle shall provide leverage for steering and be capable of withstanding a minimum force of one hundred pounds applied to each handgrip in any direction, and there shall be no back and forth, or side to side movement at the handlebar mount through the riser bushings.\n\n(b) The handlebars of each motorcycle shall not restrict the front fork movement and be capable of vertical adjustment.\n\n(c) The handlebars of each motorcycle shall provide a minimum of 18 inches between ends after final assembly.\n\n(d) Pursuant to RSA 266:77, the handlebars of each motorcycle shall not be improvised, defective or repaired.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by 11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
